A class attribute is now inferred with the values assigned to it through the
class in the module that defines it, as in ``cls.attr = value`` in a class
method or ``Klass.attr = value``, along with the value set in the class body.
Only the latter used to be inferred, so pylint reported
``unsubscriptable-object``, ``unsupported-membership-test`` and similar errors
on lazily initialized class attributes such as ``cache = None``. A value
assigned to an attribute of a parent class also no longer leaks into a
subclass that assigns the same attribute in the same scope.

Refs #3351
Closes pylint-dev/pylint#9250
Closes pylint-dev/pylint#9809
Closes pylint-dev/pylint#10082
Refs pylint-dev/pylint#3045
